# Volunteer Matching System - Project Rules

## General

This project is a Volunteer Matching Information System.

The system has two roles:
- CLIENT
- VOLUNTEER

A single User may have one or both roles.

Before implementing or modifying a feature, read the relevant documentation
under the `/docs` directory.

Do not invent new requirements or features that are not defined in the project
documentation.

## Backend Architecture

- The backend must use Python and Flask.
- Follow CQRS/MVC principles.
- Separate Commands (write operations) from Queries (read operations).
- Flask routes/controllers should remain thin.
- Business logic should not be implemented directly inside routes.
- Database access should be separated from HTTP handling.

## Frontend

- The frontend uses React with Vite.
- Keep API communication separate from UI components.
- Components should remain focused and reusable.

## Data

- PostgreSQL is the relational database.
- Do not change the database schema without checking the data model documentation.
- Event Sourcing requirements must be considered for state-changing business operations.

## AI

- AI matching is a separate concern from normal application logic.
- Structured filtering such as availability, category, and location should not be replaced by semantic matching.
- Semantic matching will use RAG and a Vector Database where appropriate.

## Development

- Implement one feature at a time.
- Prefer simple solutions appropriate for a small academic project.
- Avoid unnecessary abstractions and overengineering.
- Add or update tests when implementing business logic.
- Update relevant documentation when an architectural or functional decision changes.